### Pull request previews
{% endif %}
Each pull request that is open, not a draft and not from a bot gets a preview of the site on its own Cloudflare Worker, `{{ slug | replace('.', '-') | replace('_', '-') }}-site-pr-<number>`, deleted again when the pull request closes or turns draft ([how it works](https://github.com/simonvanlierde/project-templates/blob/main/docs/usage.md#static-site)). {% if site_on_workers %}One-time setup: run `just repo-settings`, which creates the `preview` and `production` environments, then add the secrets `CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN` (a custom token with Account > Workers Scripts: Edit{% if site_domain %}, and Zone > Workers Routes: Edit for the zone of `{{ site_domain }}`{% endif %}) and `CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID` to both, and give the Cloudflare account a workers.dev subdomain if it has none yet. Without the token, the deploy and the previews skip with a notice.{% else %}One-time setup: run `just repo-settings`, which creates the `preview` environment and sets Pages to deploy from Actions, then add the secrets `CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN` (a custom token with Account > Workers Scripts: Edit) and `CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID` to the `preview` environment, and give the Cloudflare account a workers.dev subdomain if it has none yet. Without the token, the previews skip with a notice.{% endif %} Previews are public: anyone with the address can open one.
